# GitHub Workflow (Every loop, compulsory)

All work follows this sequence. Scope: all work.

## 1. Plan

Before code changes, create or update a plan doc in `docs/<scope>/plans/` and prefer `/workflows:plan` semantics.
The plan doc is the source of intake, scope, and acceptance criteria.

Plan doc must include:
```
## Background
## Expected outcome
## Acceptance criteria
## Possible solution(s)
## References
```

## 2. Work

Checkout/create branch from `main` using `fix/<scope>-slug` or `feat/<scope>-slug`, then execute with `/workflows:work` semantics.

## 3. Review

Run `/workflows:review` style checks (automated + human) and resolve findings before merge.

## 4. Compound

Capture reusable lessons in docs/rules/skills (`/workflows:compound` semantics) so future work compounds.

## 5. PR + checks

Use conventional commits and open PR to `main`, including the active plan doc path in PR description.

**Before committing**, verify the current branch's PR is not already merged:
```
gh pr list --repo JesusFilm/forge --head "$(git branch --show-current)" --state merged --json number
```
If the result is non-empty, **stop** — do not commit or push. Create a new branch from `main` instead.

**Creating/updating PRs with multiline bodies:** Never pass `\n` escape sequences in MCP tool string parameters — they render as literal text. Always use `gh` CLI with a HEREDOC:
```
gh pr create --title "type(scope): description" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
...
EOF
)"
```
Same applies to `gh pr edit`.

## Resolving merge conflicts

**Never rebase a feature branch to resolve PR merge conflicts.** Use `git merge` instead:
```
git fetch upstream main && git merge upstream/main --no-edit
```
For `pnpm-lock.yaml` conflicts: `git checkout --theirs pnpm-lock.yaml && pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile`, then stage and commit.

Ensure all CI checks pass before marking work complete. Use `mcp_GitHub_pull_request_read` with `method: get_status` to verify. Re-run or fix failures.
Resolve all review comments with follow-up and summarize how each was handled.
